// The `c13` cell — the open divergence the (C) arc was named to close.  Was
// tests/xprod/c13_bare_lambda_to_bound.exl, a "known divergence kept for the
// fabrication scan" while the port wrongly ACCEPTED it (emitting `ex_apply2_?`,
// then a named-but-still-accepted fn-ptr).  Bound conformance now REJECTS it, so
// it is a plain parity fixture and moves to where rejection cases live.
//
// A bare non-capturing lambda has fn-ptr type, which does not implement the
// closure bound.  REJECTED, first line byte-exact with the reference.

fn apply2<F: |int|->int>(f: F, n: int) -> int { f(n) }
fn main() {
    let g = |x: int| -> int x + 1;
    println(apply2(g, 5));
    return;
}
